# No filler unless deferred to a named sprint

Prefer **one thin real path** over scaffolding that will need a later hole-patch sprint.

## Do not ship

- Placeholder digests, stub hashes, `"ok"` / `"todo"` / `unimplemented!` on production paths
- Types, traits, or helpers with **no production caller** in the same change (unless the caller is this sprint’s AC)
- Tests that only assert compile/green while the runtime boundary is unwired, mocked away, or bypassed
- “Temporary” adapters, dual implementations, or warn-only enforcement when the AC requires deny/enforce
- Docs that describe behavior the live path does not enforce

## Allowed filler — only if all are true

1. The gap is **explicitly out of scope** for this sprint’s acceptance criteria, **and**
2. A **named future sprint** (e.g. `H1-3`, `R7-1`) owns the hole — cite it in code comment and sprint/status docs, **and**
3. Status stays **Partial** (never Done) until that sprint closes with production evidence

If there is no named sprint yet, **stop and ask** before adding the stub. Do not invent silent TODOs.

## How to build instead

- Wire the chokepoint the data actually takes in this change, or cut scope and leave the unused API out
- Prefer fail-closed / honest `MissingControl` / refuse-to-run over fake success
- Tests must exercise the **production call site** (or an arch-gate that locks that wiring), not only a helper in isolation
- If AC cannot be met without later work: mark **Partial**, list unmet criteria, cite the deferral sprint — do not paper over with filler

## Pair with

`acceptance-criteria-handoff.mdc` (when something may be called Done) and `sprint-documentation.mdc` (honest Partial vs Done).
